    {
      "id": "ai-agent-orchestrator-1788684495886004",
      "data": {
        "label": "AI Agent",
        "inputs": {
          "userPrompt": "Assess the incoming procurement event using ONLY the structured evidence provided below.\r\n\r\nDo not invent missing information.\r\n\r\nThe incoming event is authoritative for event_type.\r\n\r\nDetermine:\r\n1. Whether the event is valid.\r\n2. What changed operationally.\r\n3. Whether the change is current, stale, or duplicated.\r\n4. Overall procurement risk.\r\n5. Supplier risk.\r\n6. Delivery risk.\r\n7. Capacity risk.\r\n8. Quality risk.\r\n9. Component risk.\r\n10. Whether escalation is required.\r\n11. Which downstream workflow(s) are required.\r\n12. Evidence supporting every risk assessment.\r\n13. Missing or uncertain information.\r\n\r\nFor any risk dimension where evidence is unavailable, use:\r\n\"level\": \"UNKNOWN\"\r\n\r\nand explain the missing evidence.\r\n\r\nDo not use unsupported assumptions.\r\n\r\nEVENT CONTEXT: {{$node[\"executeSubWorkflowTrigger-1788674233612006\"].json[\"items\"]}}\r\n\r\nSUPPLY / INVENTORY SQL EVIDENCE: {{$node[\"postgres.executeQuery-1789037579615001\"].json[\"items\"]}}\r\n\r Only list information as missing when it is genuinely absent from the supplied evidence.\r\n\r\nDo not list a field as missing when the supplied evidence already contains that field or an equivalent value.\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n- available_inventory is NOT missing if inventory evidence provides it.\r\n- supplier_id is NOT missing if it is present in incoming_supply.\r\n- component_id is NOT missing if it is present in the evidence.\n\r\n",
          "outputFormat": "json",
          "promptSource": "define",
          "systemPrompt": "",
          "systemMessage": "You are the Real-Time Risk Monitoring Agent for PRISM, an automotive procurement intelligence system.\n\nYour responsibility is to perform:\n1. REAL-TIME OPERATIONAL MONITORING\n2. PROCUREMENT RISK ASSESSMENT\n3. ESCALATION IDENTIFICATION\n\nYou must use ONLY the incoming event and structured database evidence supplied in the user message.\n\nDo not invent, infer, or assume:\n- supplier identity\n- component identity\n- delivery dates\n- quantities\n- inventory values\n- supplier performance\n- capacity\n- quality\n- production impact\n- historical behavior\n- alternative suppliers\n- RFQ information\n\nIf evidence is missing, return null where appropriate and list the missing information.\n\nMONITORING\n\nDetermine:\n- whether the incoming event is valid\n- the actual event type\n- whether a current operational change is supported by the evidence\n- whether the evidence appears stale\n- whether the event appears duplicated\n- which supplier/component/supply records are affected\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThe event_type supplied by the incoming event is authoritative.\nDo not replace it with another event type.\n\nRISK ASSESSMENT\n\nAssess the following independently:\n\n1. Overall procurement risk\n2. Supplier risk\n3. Delivery risk\n4. Capacity risk\n5. Quality risk\n6. Component risk\n\nFor each risk dimension:\n- provide a risk level only when supported by evidence\n- provide the evidence supporting the assessment\n- otherwise use \"UNKNOWN\"\n- do not manufacture evidence\n\nRisk levels:\nLOW\nMEDIUM\nHIGH\nCRITICAL\nUNKNOWN\n\nSUPPLIER RISK\nAssess only from supplied supplier evidence.\n\nDELIVERY RISK\nUse incoming supply status, quantity, expected delivery date, and event evidence.\n\nCAPACITY RISK\nOnly assess when actual capacity evidence is provided.\nOtherwise return UNKNOWN.\n\nQUALITY RISK\nOnly assess when actual quality evidence is provided.\nOtherwise return UNKNOWN.\n\nCOMPONENT RISK\nUse component criticality and supplied component evidence.\n\nESCALATION\n\nDetermine whether escalation is required.\n\nPossible downstream workflows:\n- PLANNING\n- SUPPLIER_INTELLIGENCE\n- DECISION_PRESCRIPTIVE\n\nDo not use descriptive phrases such as \"Procurement Review\" as workflow identifiers.\n\nUse only:\nPLANNING\nSUPPLIER_INTELLIGENCE\nDECISION_PRESCRIPTIVE\n\nThe agent must NOT:\n- select a supplier\n- negotiate with a supplier\n- approve procurement\n- create a PO\n- make the final procurement decision\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\n\nRequired output structure:\n\n{\n  \"agent\": \"REAL_TIME_RISK_MONITORING\",\n  \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n\n  \"monitoring\": {\n    \"event_type\": \"\",\n    \"event_valid\": true,\n    \"change_detected\": true,\n    \"current\": true,\n    \"stale\": false,\n    \"duplicate\": false,\n    \"operational_change\": \"\"\n  },\n\n  \"affected_entities\": {\n    \"supplier_id\": null,\n    \"component_id\": null,\n    \"rfq_id\": null\n  },\n\n  \"risk_assessment\": {\n    \"overall\": {\n      \"level\": \"LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL|UNKNOWN\",\n      \"evidence\": []\n    },\n\n    \"supplier\": {\n      \"level\": \"LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL|UNKNOWN\",\n      \"evidence\": []\n    },\n\n    \"delivery\": {\n      \"level\": \"LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL|UNKNOWN\",\n      \"evidence\": []\n    },\n\n    \"capacity\": {\n      \"level\": \"LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL|UNKNOWN\",\n      \"evidence\": []\n    },\n\n    \"quality\": {\n      \"level\": \"LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL|UNKNOWN\",\n      \"evidence\": []\n    },\n\n    \"component\": {\n      \"level\": \"LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL|UNKNOWN\",\n      \"evidence\": []\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"escalation\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"required_follow_up\": [],\n    \"reason\": \"\"\n  },\n\n  \"missing_information\": []\n}",
          "requireOutputFormat": true,
          "showSystemMessageOption": true
        },
        "toolId": "ai-agent-orchestrator",
        "toolData": {
          "id": "ai-agent-orchestrator",
          "displayName": "AI Agent",
          "category": "AI / LLM",
          "provider": "aiagent",
          "operation": "execute",
